<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alim Khan of Kokand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1811">1811</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alim Khan was a ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a> who took the title khan around 1800, turning the Kokand state into a khanate. He built a standing army that included Tajik mountain soldiers and conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> in 1808 or 1809. His harsh rule made him enemies, and he was killed in 1811 in a revolt that brought his brother Umar to power.</p></div>
